    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **34 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier so that `membershipTier` is `'GOLD'` when the owner's household has 3 or more members after the create, with the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules applying otherwise.\n\nFollowing the codebase's established pattern (derived fields are computed at create time in the controller, persisted on the `Owner` entity, and mapped to the DTO by MapStruct), the changes were:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `householdSize` field (`@Column(name = \"household_size\")`) with getter/setter, capturing the household size as a snapshot at creation time (consistent with how `namesakeCount` and `bulkSignupWarning` work).\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 set `owner.setHouseholdSize(householdMembers.size() + 1)`. `householdMembers` is the set of pre-existing owners sharing the same normalized last name + address (i.e. the same deterministic `householdId`), so `+1` for the owner being created gives the size after this create.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 updated the `membershipTier` expression so GOLD takes precedence: `householdSize >= 3` \u2192 `GOLD`; else the original `namesakeCount == 0 && email present` \u2192 `SILVER`; else `BRONZE`.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `GOLD` to the `membershipTier` enum (so the generated `MembershipTierEnum.GOLD` exists) and updated the field description.\n\n5. **DB schemas** (h2, hsqldb, postgres, mysql) \u2014 added the `household_size` column. Tests run on the hsqldb schema; the others were updated for parity.\n\nThe tier is derived purely from persisted entity state, so it reproduces correctly when the owner is re-read via `GET /api/owners/{id}` (which the acceptance test relies on).",
